(4899289, 710076, 96762, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by colorcarnival:</b></div><hr/><i> after I read the last comment you received, a word popped into my head that I have not used since grade school:  whir-dey... and we used it to put emphasis on all meanings behind the word "DUH".  It''s too bad that someone could not tell from the image that you had a glowing duck.  I''m sure that if you had titled it "duck" that it would have been much clearer and garnered you some more votes.  Think about it, man...<br/> <br/>I do like the simplicity of this photo and the duck has a nice glow about it too. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Obviously you missed the whole point of my comment too.   lol</td>', 'Originally posted by colorcarnival: after I read the last comment you received, a word popped into my head that I have not used since grade school:  whir-dey... and we used it to put emphasis on all meanings behind the word "DUH".  It''s too bad that someone could not tell from the image that you had a glowing duck.  I''m sure that if you had titled it "duck" that it would have been much clearer and garnered you some more votes.  Think about it, man... I do like the simplicity of this photo and the duck has a nice glow about it too.   Obviously you missed the whole point of my comment too.   lol', '2008-08-20 02:53:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4899343, 710128, 47541, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the PM, it certainly gives insight into your shot:<br/> <br/>****************<br/>Hi Gerry<br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment on my Duck You! entry.<br/> <br/>In fact my score has gone up, nice and steadily.<br/> <br/>You see, I don''t shoot stuff that wins.  What will win is a pleasingly composed shot of a ducky, saturtated to the eyeballs, probably clutched in a child''s hand or balanced on their head or something similar.<br/> <br/>Sorry, but just the thought of shooting something so boringly predictable puts me to sleep.  But hey, if you want to win, that''s the kind of stuff they want to see.<br/> <br/>I will likely never win a challenge, and I really don''t give a rat''s arse if I don''t. Or in this case, the arse of a ducky stuck headfirst into a goldfish bowl filled with whipped blue jello.<br/> <br/>I joined this site to compete, learn, and have fun, and I am accomplishing all those goals by shooting what I want, not what the dpc vox populi want to see.<br/> <br/>If you visit my homepage, you''ll see that I belong to Team Suck.  And as TS is home to many ribbon winners - levyj413, colorcarnival, Melethia, NikonJeb, basssman7, Doyle, SaraR, even silverfoxxx - we are by no means a bunch of talentless photogs.<br/> <br/>So, maybe before thinking that mentioning someone''s score likely isn''t all that hight, maybe you should stop and think: who are you really shooting for, dpc? Or yourself?<br/> <br/>Sleep on it.<br/> <br/>Peace and love,<br/> <br/>Susan<br/> <br/>Peace and love,<br/> <br/><i>Edit because I can''t spell correctly the first time :(</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-20 02:38:27.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the PM, it certainly gives insight into your shot: ****************Hi Gerry Thanks for your comment on my Duck You! entry. In fact my score has gone up, nice and steadily. You see, I don''t shoot stuff that wins.  What will win is a pleasingly composed shot of a ducky, saturtated to the eyeballs, probably clutched in a child''s hand or balanced on their head or something similar. Sorry, but just the thought of shooting something so boringly predictable puts me to sleep.  But hey, if you want to win, that''s the kind of stuff they want to see. I will likely never win a challenge, and I really don''t give a rat''s arse if I don''t. Or in this case, the arse of a ducky stuck headfirst into a goldfish bowl filled with whipped blue jello. I joined this site to compete, learn, and have fun, and I am accomplishing all those goals by shooting what I want, not what the dpc vox populi want to see. If you visit my homepage, you''ll see that I belong to Team Suck.  And as TS is home to many ribbon winners - levyj413, colorcarnival, Melethia, NikonJeb, basssman7, Doyle, SaraR, even silverfoxxx - we are by no means a bunch of talentless photogs. So, maybe before thinking that mentioning someone''s score likely isn''t all that hight, maybe you should stop and think: who are you really shooting for, dpc? Or yourself? Sleep on it. Peace and love, Susan Peace and love, Edit because I can''t spell correctly the first time :(', '2008-08-20 03:25:57.000000', '2008-08-20 03:38:27.000000', 0),
