(4899899, 710076, 61961, '<td valign="top">Ok, ladies, take it outside.  ;-D<br/> <br/>Seriously, thank you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67697" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">colorcarnival</a> for your assessment (which pretty much matched my first reaction), and thank you <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=96762" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mstone</a> for expressing your feelings.  Some people don''t like obvious titles, some people don''t like contrived ones, and now I''ve learned some people don''t like it when there isn''t a title at all.  There have been long debates in the forums on the subject.  I prefer the "First, let the photo speak for itself" way.</td>', 'Ok, ladies, take it outside.  ;-D Seriously, thank you  colorcarnival for your assessment (which pretty much matched my first reaction), and thank you  mstone for expressing your feelings.  Some people don''t like obvious titles, some people don''t like contrived ones, and now I''ve learned some people don''t like it when there isn''t a title at all.  There have been long debates in the forums on the subject.  I prefer the "First, let the photo speak for itself" way.', '2008-08-20 09:55:07.000000', NULL, 0),
